\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  FOCUS: Twisting The Yen Back Down Again\b0\par\par\uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2011\par 12:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat keeps yen from rising more\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  Twist should have helped the dollar higher\par \par \uc2 --Bank of Japan may be biding time until next meeting\par \par \uc2 By Nicholas Hastings\par \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Tokyo should get its way soon--at least where the yen is concerned.\par \par \uc2 For months, financial markets have watched Japan take the pain of a strong yen with the country accepting that the yen's safe-haven status made \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly impossible.\par \par \uc2 After tumbling from over Y81 in early July to under Y76 in the middle of August, the dollar settled into a fairly narrow trading range between Y76 and Y78 as the threat of Bank of Japan action helped to reduce safe-haven flows.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Japan has had to sit by as central banks of other major economies poured more liquidity into their markets and made their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  even less attractive relative to the yen.\par \par \uc2 Probably, the only reason that the yen hasn't risen any more in recent weeks is that the Bank of Japan, under the management of a new government in Tokyo, has kept the markets guessing about when and if it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chances are they may not have to wait too much longer as support for the yen could start to fade.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve's introduction of the so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 Operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  Twist could help with some of this.\par \par \uc2 The yen's performance against the dollar has long been correlated with the yield spread between two-year Japanese and U.S. swaps. The introduction of twist, in which the Fed drove short-term yields lower compared with long-term yields on the U.S. Treasury curve, should have helped to drive the dollar as high as Y80, according to \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, because of continued safe-haven flows the pair has yet to make that move.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan's decision Friday to leave its interest rates unchanged at 0%-0.1% and only extend its measures for helping financial institutions in disaster areas showed it is in no hurry.\par \par \uc2 But, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is looking for moderate growth to resume, it expressed concerns about the impact the global slowdown will have on Japan's future.\par \par \uc2 Given the growing stress that a strong yen is putting on Japan's corporate sector, pressure on the Bank of Japan to act is increasing.\par \par \uc2 The fact that the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  recently succeeded in driving its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back down despite heavy safe-haven flows in the Swiss franc's favor is only contributing to speculation that it is now Japan's turn to act by adopting its own unorthodox policies to keep the yen competitive.\par \par \uc2 A variety of analysts suggest that this could come at the bank's next meeting at the end of this month, especially if hopes about the global economy have improved and some of the safe-haven flows have started to subside.\par \par \uc2 Given that the two-year swap spread is also in the dollar's favor, this would make any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that much easier for the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the chances of the dollar being pushed back up to Y80 that much greater.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg TNI FRX POV\par \par \uc2 Reuters USD/DJ\par \par \uc2 Thomson P/1066 or P/1074\par \par \uc2 (Nicholas Hastings is a Senior Correspondent in London for Dow Jones Newswires who has written about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than 20 years. He previously covered a variety of markets, including equities, fixed income, commodities and energy. He can be contacted on +44-20-7842-9493 or at (nick.hastings@dowjones.com) [ 07-10-11 1024GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1066   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111007e7a7000qg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
