\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Yen strength likely to persist through euro crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2011\par 16:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Full data or\par \par \uc2 * Euro/yen to remain below 110 level for next 12 mths\par \par \uc2 * Dlr/yen in 77-78 range for next six months\par \par \uc2 * Euro/chf at 1.21 level for next six months\par \par \uc2 By Anooja Debnath\par \par \uc2 BANGALORE, Oct 5 (Reuters) - The Japanese yen will remain firm against the dollar and relatively so against the euro so long as it there is no clear resolution to the euro zone crisis, according to a Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 The poll of around 60 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists taken this week sees dollar/yen at 77 in a month, 78\par \par \uc2 in six months and 80 in a year, little changed from September's poll.\par \par \uc2 "In the longer term it will remain range bound ... between 75-80, with probably preference to the downside," said Chris Walker, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Against the euro , the yen is expected to firm to 101.6 in one month from 102.3 on Wednesday. It is then expected to slip by less than forecast in last month's poll, to 104.1 in six months and 109.1 in a year.\par \par \uc2 The September consensus was for 110.0 yen per euro in one month, 112.0 in six and 114.1 in a year.\par \par \uc2 The battered common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen by around six percent since August and dropped to a decade low versus the yen to 101.946 in September.\par \par \uc2 "We don't expect an ever-falling euro but in the short term we see a downside," said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 The euro is under pressure from the threat of a Greek default and Europe still seemingly far from a concrete solution to its debt woes. The rise in the yen in turn hurts Japanese exporters in an economy that's already struggling.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa offered a bleak assessment of the country's economic outlook on Wednesday as Europe's debt crisis hurts stock markets and keeps the safe-haven yen at stubbornly high levels.\par \par \uc2 Annualised monthly yen volatility fell to 6.0 percent in September compared to 11.7 percent in August. It is predicted to rise slightly to 7.2 percent in October.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BoJ) and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MoF)\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in six years in September 2010 to stem the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo spent 4.5 trillion yen in early August and while the fall in dollar/yen might have stalled, it has remained in the 76-77 range since then.\par \par \uc2 Whether the BoJ and MoF will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again soon is unclear. But Yamamoto says if euro/yen fell below 100 it will cause the Nikkei to fall below 8,000 and that might prompt more action by the authorities.\par \par \uc2 Forecast medians for the Swiss franc versus the euro\par \par \uc2 were at 1.21 in the one- and six-month horizon before rising to 1.24 in a year, around the same levels seen in September's poll.\par \par \uc2 In September the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  said it would no longer tolerate an exchange rate below 1.20 francs to the euro and would defend the target by buying other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in unlimited amounts.\par \par \uc2 For other stories from the poll click on )\par \par \uc2 (Polling by Ruby Cherian and Namrata Anchan)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -JPY/POLL (EMBARGO 1320 GMT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111008e7a5000ft\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
