\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Japan MOF Official: Azumi Told ECB Noyer That Strong Yen Impeding Japan Industries\b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2011\par 11:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 3 Oct 2011 05:24 EDT *DJ  Japan MOF Official: ECB Noyer Told Azumi Surprised By Japan Manufacturers' Recovery From Quake\par \par \uc2 3 Oct 2011 05:26 EDT *DJ  Japan MOF Official: Azumi Told Noyer Europe Needs To Send Strong Message On Greece At G-20\par \par \uc2 3 Oct 2011 05:54 EDT DJ  Japan Finance Minister Tells ECB Noyer Of Concerns Over Yen\par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister conveyed his concerns over the strong yen to France's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief on Monday, a Japanese finance ministry official said, as Tokyo continues to try to rally international support for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 At their 30-minute meeting earlier in the day, Jun Azumi told Christian Noyer, a member of the ECB's board of governors and the Bank of France governor, that the strong yen is "a drag on Japan's main industries, such as automobile makers," the official said.\par \par \uc2 In response, Noyer told Azumi that he had been surprised by the strong recovery of Japanese manufacturers from the March 11 earthquake and tsunami, the Japanese official said.\par \par \uc2 The difference in tone could add to speculation that other advanced nations, particularly in Europe, are unwilling to back market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen for the benefit of Japanese exporters.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early August drew complaints from Europe and the U.S.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi 