\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  to boost  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  fund by 15 trln yen\b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2011\par 03:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Finmin says to extend period for required trader \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporting to Dec\par \par \uc2  * Finmin vows to take firm action if needed, won't rule out any steps on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2  By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will boost its war chest for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 15 trillion yen ($195 billion) to give itself more leeway in case it needs step into the market again to counter speculators pushing up the yen, Finance Minister Jun Azumi said on Friday.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make necessary tweaks to the state budget's general rules when it compiles a third extra budget next month for the current fiscal year to March, in order to raise the borrowing limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2  The ministry will also extend until December a rule requiring \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders to report on trading volumes, Azumi told reporters after a cabinet meeting, saying the emergency step had been effective to a certain extent since it was put in place last month.\par \par \uc2  The scheme, due to expire on Friday, requires major financial institutions operating in Japan to report on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions held by dealers on a daily basis to strengthen monitoring of markets and ensure stability.\par \par \uc2  "We'll strengthen monitoring in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and flexibly monitor speculative moves," Azumi said. "We won't rule out any measures and will take decisive steps if necessary."\par \par \uc2  In the 2011/12 state budget, the government has set a borrowing limit of 150 trillion yen for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  special account.\par \par \uc2  The proposed change would increase that amount to 165 trillion yen. With 119 trillion yen already having been used, that would leave 46 trillion yen still available for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a record amount, Azumi said.\par \par \uc2  The extra budget, due to be compiled next month and containing the bulk of planned spending for post-quake reconstruction, will then be submitted to parliament, where it faces political wrangling with the opposition-controlled upper house.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market twice on its own and once jointly with other Group of Seven nations over the past year to stem a rise in the yen that has damaged its crucial export sector and threatened to derail the country's economic recovery.\par \par \uc2  The government's forays into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market led to an increase in the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related borrowing, mainly via financing bills (FBs) issued specifically to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to 119 trillion yen.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 76.840 Japanese Yen) \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Edmund Klamann)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/AZUMI  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111003e79u0001d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
