\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 30\b0\par\par\uc2 1,807 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2011\par 09:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: S&P, FITCH DOWNGRADE NEW ZEALAND, CITING EXTERNAL DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services and Fitch Ratings both downgraded New Zealand's government debt Friday, citing its worsening external-debt position and the costs of earthquake recovery. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO BOOST YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WAR CHEST \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister sent out a fresh warning against the yen's persistent strength on Friday, with a plan to expand the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war chest to record levels and a vow to take "decisive measures" to limit the yen's rise. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: CHINA SAFE REVISES DOWN 1H CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator on Friday revised down its estimate of China's current account surplus in the first half of the year to $87.8 billion, from a previous estimate of $98.4 billion. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: HSBC CHINA PMI STEADY IN SEPTEMBER VS. AUGUST AT 49.9 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The final HSBC China Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index, a gauge of nationwide manufacturing activity, was unchanged at 49.9 in September compared with 49.9 in August, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: YUAN HITS LOW END OF TRADING BAND FOR 3RD CONSECUTIVE DAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan hit the low end of its daily trading band against the U.S. dollar Friday for the third consecutive session, as the scramble for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  intensified amid persistent demand from Chinese importers and investors wary of the growing global economic uncertainties. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: JAPAN OUTPUT CONTINUES POST-QUAKE RECOVERY, BUT ROUGH ROAD AHEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production continued to get back on its feet after the March 11 earthquake and tsunami, rising for the fifth straight month in August as the transportation, steel, and electronic parts and devices sectors dialed up output. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOVERNOR: CAUTION OVER PROSPECTS FOR GLOBAL ECONOMY INCREASING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Friday caution over the prospects for the global economy is increasing as the U.S. economic slowdown has become more evident, while concerns about the euro-zone debt crisis persist. (published 0631 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: KOREA AUGUST INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT WEAKER THAN EXPECTED; MOMENTUM SLOWING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's industrial output rose at a slower-than-expected pace in August as production of semiconductors and electronics devices weakened, government data showed Friday, indicating slowing growth momentum for Asia's fourth-largest economy as global uncertainties shake markets. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CIC EXECUTIVE: CHINA CAN'T BUY EURO-ZONE ASSETS WITHOUT CLEAR PICTURE OF SOLUTIONS -XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China can't be expected to buy assets in the euro zone without seeing a clear picture of the solutions to the region's sovereign debt problems, the state-run Xinhua News Agency reported Friday, citing Jin Liqun, chairman of \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s supervisory board. (published 0113 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA WARNS MARKET TURMOIL WILL HIT TAX REVENUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's government said Friday that it expects weaker revenues due to the ongoing shakeout of global markets, but stuck by a pledge to return a balanced budget in the 2012-13 fiscal year. (published 0138 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : INFLATION TO STAY WITHIN 2011 TARGET DESPITE TYPHOONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday that despite recent typhoons that have damaged large areas of farm land, inflation should remain within its target range. (published 0506 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: AUSTRALIA'S RBA TO KEEP RATES STEADY TUES -ECONOMISTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to keep interest rates on hold at a policy meeting Tuesday, with market expectations of aggressive interest rate cuts over the next year likely to be challenged by the bank's accompanying statement. (published 0607 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDONESIA SEPT CPI LIKELY +4.77% ON YEAR, +0.39% ON MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's inflation rate will likely ease in September, but this will unlikely prompt the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lower its policy rate when it next meets Oct. 11 as a cut would put further downward pressure on the rupiah. (published 0159 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDONESIA AUGUST TRADE SURPLUS LIKELY WIDENED TO $1.87 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia likely posted a wider trade surplus in August than in July on resilient demand for its commodities globally, economists said. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LIKELY TO PAUSE TIGHTENING UNTIL 2Q 2012 - DJ POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected to stand pat on key interest rates at least for the next nine months, as the enervating global economic outlook outweighs the need to normalize ultra-low domestic lending costs that have contributed to a sizzling property market. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: MINMETALS TO BUY ANVIL MINING FOR C$1.33 BLN CASH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Minmetals Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . offered to buy Congo-focused copper miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anvil Mining Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for C$1.33 billion in cash Friday, a move that shows Chinese companies remain willing to invest in risky locations despite a recent fall in commodity prices. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN COURT TELLS APPLE, SAMSUNG TO SIMPLIFY CASES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An Australian court said Friday that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will have to simplify their cases if the court is to rule by next week on a temporary injunction on Samsung's tablet release in Australia. (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOYO SEIKAN: TO BUY US FIRM STOLLE MACHINERY FOR ABOUT $775M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bolstered by the strong yen, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyo Seikan Kaisha Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that it will buy U.S. can-making machinery firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stolle Machinery Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for about Y59.7 billion, or $775 million. (published 0007 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SMBC TO MAKE CONSUMER LENDER PROMISE WHOLLY OWNED UNIT -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to make its troubled consumer lending subsidiary Promise Co. a wholly owned unit, a person familiar with the matter said Friday, as it looks to revitalize a business hit hard by losses from repaying overcharged interest to borrowers. (published 0317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: STANCHART CEO WARNS TIGHTER CAPITAL RULES MIGHT HURT REAL ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Friday called for closer coordination between regulatory bodies around the globe, warning that tighter banking requirements could result in slower economic growth. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TELECOM: TELEBONDS STOCKHOLDERS APPROVE DEMERGER EXTRAORDINARY RESOLUTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telecom Corp. of New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  is one step closer to spinning off its infrastructure unit after the company's bond holders approved the plan to split into two listed companies. (published 2334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CAPITAMALLS ASIA GETS INITIAL APPROVAL FOR HONG KONG SECONDARY LISTING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shopping mall developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 CapitaMalls Asia Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has received approval-in-principle to proceed with a secondary listing on the Hong Kong stock exchange, jumping a key hurdle in its plans for tapping Asia's largest capital markets to fuel growth in China. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANEKA TAMBANG 1H NET PROFIT IDR1.036 TLN VS IDR853.52 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold and nickel producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Aneka Tambang\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday its first-half audited net profit rose 21%. (published 0034 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHAODA SAYS EXECS DENY INSIDER DEALING CHARGES MADE BY HK GOVERNMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chaoda Modern Agriculture Ltd. said Friday its chairman and chief financial officer deny having engaged in insider dealing as the Hong Kong government has alleged, and stressed that the proceedings against its executives won't have any material impact on the company's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or financial position. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RELIANCE ANIL AMBANI GROUP DENIES ROLE IN TELECOM SCAM; SHARES SLUMP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian billionaire Anil Ambani's Reliance Group Friday denied that any of the group companies, including \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance Telecom Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., illegally benefited from the 2008 sale of telecommunication licenses that has now turned into the country's biggest corruption scandal. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RELIANCE CAPITAL GETS RBI NOD FOR STAKE SALE IN LIFE INSURANCE UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reliance Capital Ltd. said Friday it has received the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 's approval for a proposed stake sale in its life insurance unit to Japan-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nippon Life Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BUMI ARMADA: SIGNED MYR1.46 BLN FPSO CONTRACT WITH APACHE ENERGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bumi Armada Bhd., a Malaysian oil and gas service provider, said Friday that it has signed a MYR1.46 billion contract to provide \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apache Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  with a floating production, storage and offloading vessel. (published 0529 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JOLLIBEE BUYS 54% OF FIRM HOLDING LOCAL BURGER KING FRANCHISE FOR PHP65.5 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jollibee Foods Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the Philippines' largest fastfood firm by sales, said Friday it has acquired a majority stake for PHP65.5 million in the local firm that holds the franchise to operate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Burger King\f28 \uc2 \f2  in the country. (published 0622 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY LOWER, EURO FALLS AS CAUTION PERSISTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stocks were mostly lower in choppy trade Friday and the euro lost ground, as many markets appeared set to end September in the red after some of the heaviest selloffs in the period since the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers\f28 \uc2 \f2  collapse in 2008. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: G20 SETS UP INFORMATION SYSTEM TO MANAGE FOOD PRICE VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of 20 industrialized and emerging nations will launch an agricultural markets information system, or AMIS, to manage volatility in food prices and issue alerts ahead of potential crisis situations, a senior United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization official said. (published 0607 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOVT PANEL TO URGE 7400 JOB CUTS AT TEPCO, UTILITY MAY BE UNABLE TO REPAY DEBTS -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 30-09-11 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A government panel will recommend in an upcoming report that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . cuts 7,400 jobs by March 2014, while indicating that the troubled utility may be unable to repay some of its debts to financial institutions, the Yomiuri Shimbun reported in its Wednesday morning edition. (published 0104 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WESFARMERS AGREES TO SELL PREMIER COAL FOR A$296.8M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian retail-to-chemicals conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wesfarmers Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will sell its Premier Coal business in the state of Western Australia to Chinese coal miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yanzhou Coal Mining Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for A$296.8 million, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wesfarmers\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 2244 GMT Tuesday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL GRAIN OUTPUT TO REMAIN VOLATILE IN 4Q; CORRECTION DUE TO DEMAND -FAO OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global grain prices will remain volatile in the next quarter, a senior United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization official said, attributing the latest downward correction mainly to weakening demand amid economic recession rather than to any surplus stocks. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WESTERN AUSTRALIA WHEAT CROP LIKELY MORE THAN 9 MLN TONS -ANZ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wheat production in Western Australia state this crop year will likely exceed 9.0 million metric tons, making it one of the biggest crops on record, helped by above average rainfall in September, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a forecast Friday. (published 0204 GMT) [ 30-09-11 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110930e79u000gz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
