\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro relieved by EU hopes, yen on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  watch\b0\par\par\uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2011\par 01:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Euro off 8-month trough vs USD & decade low vs yen\par \par \uc2 * Market talking of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week\par \par \uc2 * Parliamentary votes on EFSF, Greek austerity still loom\par \par \uc2 By Cecile Lefort\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, Sept 27 (Reuters) - The euro held gains in early Asia on Tuesday, following a sudden turnaround in investor mood from extreme skepticism to tentative optimism that Europe was really putting a plan together to deal with its debt and banking crisis.\par \par \uc2 The euro was last at $1.3516 , having rallied from an eight-month low of $1.3360 on Monday. It was steady against the yen at 103.17 , having bounced from a fresh decade low at 101.90 yen.\par \par \uc2 A steady drip feed of reports about how euro zone authorities were considering bolder steps to tackle their problems lifted the mood, though many hurdles lie ahead.\par \par \uc2 CNBC said one plan involves setting up a special purpose vehicle to buy distressed debt from banks and issuing them with new paper that could be exchanged with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB).\par \par \uc2 While an ECB official confirmed the 440 billion euros-EFSF would likely be increased, another ECB member also hinted at a coming rate cut and extended lending \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Markets are getting more confident around some action plan in Europe, which is positive, but on the other side, markets are also looking for more policy easing from the ECB, which is negative," said Greg Gibbs, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBS in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 "The combination of both will leave the euro caught in the middle somewhere."\par \par \uc2 For now support is found at $1.3470, ahead of a more solid floor at $1.3430-40, while resistance is seen at $1.3585, then $1.3630.\par \par \uc2 The euro zone is still facing plenty of hurdles, including votes this week in Finland and Germany on the earlier EFSF structure. The Greek government votes Tuesday on new austerity measures needed to secure aid.\par \par \uc2 However, talk of the new action plan seemed enough to ease the ultra-bearishness of investors and trigger a rebound in riskier assets such as commodities and stocks.\par \par \uc2 Copper had an amazing day, ending up 2 percent higher after crashing more than 6 percent at one stage.\par \par \uc2 Risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also had a wild ride with the Aussie\par \par \uc2 bouncing back to $0.9838, from a 10-month trough of $0.9622.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index edged down 0.35 percent to 78.088, after hitting an eight-month peak of 78.863.\par \par \uc2 The dollar remained stuck against the yen at 76.36 , though traders reported growing talk \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week ahead of the end of their financial half-year. The yen has gained nearly 6 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Early Tuesday, Japan's government said it wants to bring forward steps to ease the pain some companies feel from a stronger yen and enact the measures before it completes an extra budget to fund reconstruction spending.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Wayne Cole)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110926e79q001l1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
