\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan warns of  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  action, complains to G20 of yen rise\b0\par\par\uc2 836 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2011\par 01:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Azumi tells G20 yen rise hurting Japan economy\par \par \uc2  * BOJ head also says strong yen a drag to growth\par \par \uc2  * Emerging nations share Japan concern on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility\par \par \uc2  * BOJ under heat as yen rise could hurt sentiment \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, detail)\par \par \uc2  By Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Sept 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeated its threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and told its G20 counterparts the strong yen was hurting its economy, adding that its displeasure over market volatility was shared by emerging economies hit by sharp falls in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Both the finance minister and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said they complained at the G20 gathering that recent yen rises were threatening Japan's recovery, a sign that Tokyo pushed hard to have the group's communique warn against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves -- a line usually saved for G7 advanced nations with big and liquid capital markets.\par \par \uc2  "Yen rises have been a severe drag on Japan's economy since August, so I expressed concern over the moves," Finance Minister Jun Azumi told a news conference after the dinner meeting of G20 finance leaders on Thursday.\par \par \uc2  It is highly unusual for the G20 to debate specifically about \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or mention it in its communique.\par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa also kept alive expectations of further monetary easing, saying that yen rises had adverse effects on the country's economy and that he was keenly aware of heightening uncertainty on global growth.\par \par \uc2  The yen edged up near an all-time high hit in August, attracting demand as a safe haven as world stocks were battered by weak data from China, a grim economic outlook from the Federal Reserve and the escalating euro-zone debt crisis.\par \par \uc2  "We've been saying all along that we will take decisive action against speculative, excessive yen rises that deviate from economic fundamentals," Azumi told reporters upon his arrival to attend the G20 gathering.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  unilaterally in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and eased monetary policy last month to stem sharp rises in the yen that threatened to derail a fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2  It has held off from stepping into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since then. But its policymakers have persisted with verbal warnings to the market against pushing the yen up too far, worried about damages from yen rises as the export-reliant economy recovers from the March earthquake.\par \par \uc2  The yen stood around 76.29 to the dollar on Thursday, not far away from its historical high of 75.94 hit last month.\par \par \uc2  While G7 advanced economies have offered a cool response to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month, a senior IMF official said each country reserves the right to step into the market if moves in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were volatile. \par \par \uc2  Japan was not alone this time in fretting about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility.\par \par \uc2  The communique's warning on excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves reflected not just Japan's view but also that of emerging nations suffering from sharp falls in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a senior Japanese finance ministry said.\par \par \uc2  The escalating euro zone debt problems and fears of a global recession have heightened risk aversion and triggered an outflow of funds from some emerging economies. Brazil, for one, unexpectedly acted to halt a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slide that could cause a spurt in inflation.\par \par \uc2  BOJ FACES HEAT\par \par \uc2  Under pressure from investors to show action, finance ministers and central bankers gathered in Washington for the G20 economies pledged on Thursday to take all steps needed to prevent Europe's debt crisis from undermining banks, and said the euro zone's rescue fund would be bolstered.\par \par \uc2  Japan, like other countries, is ready to help but on condition that Europe agrees on concrete steps to deal with the problem and rescue troubled countries like Greece.\par \par \uc2  Tokyo may offer additional support including continued buying of bonds issued by the euro zone's rescue fund, if the need for funds increases unexpectedly, Azumi said.\par \par \uc2  "What's first and foremost is for Europe to stabilise the situation, including the crisis in Greece," he said. "If confidence in the euro is restored, the yen's rises will ease."\par \par \uc2  Persistent yen rises and tumbling global stocks add pressure on the Bank of Japan for further monetary easing, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has argued that it pre-empted risks to growth by boosting asset purchases in August.\par \par \uc2  Still, many analysts expect it to ease policy again next month, as its recent action has been largely triggered by sharp rises in the yen accompanied by stock price falls.\par \par \uc2  Shirakawa stuck to his view that Japan's economy was recovering steadily with output and exports bouncing back to levels before the March quake as companies restore supply chains hit by the disaster.\par \par \uc2  But he said yen rises were hurting Japan's economy and uncertainty over the global outlook could weaken demand for its exports.\par \par \uc2  "As we have mentioned in August, the BOJ is keenly aware of uncertainty over the global economy," Shirakawa said. \par \par \uc2 (Editing by Chizu Nomiyama and Kavita Chandran)\par \par \uc2 G20/JAPAN (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110925e79m000pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
