\par\par \b \uc2 Strong Yen To Spur More M&A, Consolidation In Japan: \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's Koll\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chana R. Schoenberger   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2011\par 22:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Japanese companies will use the strengthening yen to buy assets overseas as the country comes back from March's natural disasters, Jesper Koll, head of Japanese equity research at \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2 , told Dow Jones Newswires on Wednesday. He said the bank forecasts the yen will reach Y70 against the dollar, setting a new record.\par \par \uc2 The earthquake, tsunami and nuclear crisis that hit Japan in March--dubbed "3/11" within the country--spurred businesses to carry out long-envisioned expansions, Koll said. "What 3/11 did was [it] brought out of the drawers the action plans," sparking acquisitions abroad as well as consolidation at home, he said. "3/11 really was a catalyst for the next wave of Japan's globalization."\par \par \uc2 Corporate Japan is one of the leading globalizers, Koll said, citing the automotive sector, responsible for about one third of the Japan's gross domestic product. Japanese auto makers have about 60% of their production capacity overseas, mitigating the strength of the yen, he said.\par \par \uc2 While a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurts exporters, it helps importers, as well as the service sector. Over the past few years, for instance, Japanese retailers have restructured, leaving four major department stores where once there were nine. Winners in retail: electronics maker \uc2 Yamada Denki Co\uc2 . (9831.TO), convenience store chain \uc2 Lawson Inc\uc2 . (2651.TO) and clothing store Uniqlo, all of which have expanded to other countries, including China.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely finished \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, which it has done twice in the past year to little effect, Koll said. He doubts the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will change its policies, at least until February 2013, when a new governor is scheduled to take the reins. A parliamentary bill designed to make the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more accountable to legislators and more sensitive to inflation and unemployment has stalled after the March disasters shifted national priorities.\par \par \uc2 Koll noted that the yen was trading around Y280 against the dollar when he moved to Japan some 25 years ago. With productivity growing steadily in Japan all through that period, he said, it is no surprise that the yen has appreciated as well.\par \par \uc2 -By Chana R. Schoenberger, Dow Jones Newswires;\par \par \uc2 212-416-4803; chana.schoenberger@dowjones.com [ 09-21-11 1644ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110921e79l000vv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
