\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Falls After S&P Downgrades Italy\b0\par\par\uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2011\par 02:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Euro falls sharply after S&P downgrades Italy\par \par \uc2 -- Talks with Greece to continue after failing to reach deal on Monday\par \par \uc2 -- Yen pulls back from one-month high against dollar hit overnight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Kosaku Narioka \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The euro fell sharply Tuesday in early Asian trade after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  announced a downgrade of Italy, while talks on Greece failed to reach an agreement needed to ensure new loans.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The picture in Europe, full stop, is not getting any better. They can patch up any way they want the Greek situation but the problem is going to persist. If it doesn't persist in Greece, it will persist in Portugal or Ireland, or Italy or Spain," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 HiFX\f28 \uc2 \f2  senior trader Stuart Ive in Auckland.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 S&P lowered Italy's sovereign debt rating to A from A+, citing weak economic growth and growing political problems, adding that it maintained a negative outlook. The move came soon after Moody's Investors Service on Friday said it was delaying any action on a possible downgrade of its own much higher Aa2 rating for up to a month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro fell sharply on the S&P announcement and at 2350 GMT was trading at $1.3619, down from $1.3685 in late New York trade Monday, according to data from EBS. It also fell to Y104.38 from Y104.89.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The S&P news added to a generally negative outlook for the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over worries about Greece. Talks with the European Union, International Monetary Fund and the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to discuss the country's compliance with the terms of a bailout agreement failed to reach an agreement Monday for additional funding, but they are to resume later Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Greek newspaper Kathimerini reported Monday that Greek Prime Minister George Papandreou is considering a referendum on whether the country should exit the euro zone. A Greek government official, speaking to Dow Jones Newswires, denied the report and dismissed talk of such a referendum as "comical."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior dealer at a major Japanese bank said that amid all the uncertainty, the euro will likely swing in a wide range of $1.3500 to $1.3700 and Y103.00 to Y105.00 during the day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen was somewhat weaker against the dollar, meanwhile, with markets continuing to look for renewed yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The dollar was at Y76.64. In New York trade on Monday, it had hit a one-month low of Y76.32 before ending the day at Y76.59.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Korean won was sharply lower against the dollar after the Italy downgrade. The greenback rose to KRW1,148.00, its highest since December 2010, up from KRW1,137.00 late Monday. A South Korean official said that the won's recent decline appeared to be excessive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pairs the dollar was at CHF0.8856 against the Swiss franc from CHF0.8819. The U.K. pound was at $1.5668 from $1.5699. The ICE Dollar Index was at 77.374 from 76.599.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 1950 EDT / 2350 GMT \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            76.64-66       76.56-61  +0.08    76.67    76.58  -5.51 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.3617-20      1.3685-88  -0.50   1.3688   1.3600  +1.70 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5665-70      1.5702-08  -0.24   1.5704   1.5658  +0.38 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.8853-60      0.8818-22  +0.41   0.8867   0.8820  -5.28 \par USD/CAD Canada          0.9927-32      0.9902-07  +0.25   0.9940   0.9896  -0.18 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0180-84      1.0219-25  -0.39   1.0226   1.0150  -0.51 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.8200-06      0.8247-52  -0.56   0.8249   0.8180  +5.22 \par  \par Euro Rate \par EUR/JPY Japan           104.34-38      104.80-87  -0.45   104.80   104.16  -3.94 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Kosaku Narioka, Dow Jones Newswires; 81-3-6269-2784; kosakuk.narioka@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Rebecca Howard in Wellington contributed to this article. [ 09-19-11 2050ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020110920e79k00004\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
