\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-BOJ FOCUS-BOJ to resist pressure to be as bold as Swiss\b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara   \par \uc2 940 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2011\par 03:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Repeats story filed on Tuesday, adds dropped word in paragraph 3)\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 13 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan is relieved Switzerland's radical move to weaken the franc so far has not unleashed a flood of yen buy orders, but fears it will come under pressure from politicians to do something similarly dramatic if the yen spikes again.\par \par \uc2  The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set an exchange rate cap on the soaring franc and pledged to defend it with unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, fanning talk that some risk-averse investors who sought safety in the franc could turn to the yen instead.\par \par \uc2  So far the yen has stayed below its record high hit in mid-August, but remains well above exporters' comfort levels and the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has signalled its readiness to ease policy again to help exporters as global growth falters.\par \par \uc2  But it would probably do it by further expanding its asset buying programme and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already lining up arguments why "going Swiss" is neither possible nor necessary.\par \par \uc2  "Japan is different from Switzerland because the yen is a G3 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a source familiar with the BOJ's thinking.\par \par \uc2  "Just because Switzerland is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not mean it's become easier for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do the same. It's not that simple."\par \par \uc2  First, unlike the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 , the BOJ does not have jurisdiction over exchange-rate policy and only acts as an agent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Secondly, the Japanese economy is five times the size of Switzerland's and the yen's trading volume far exceeds that of the franc, which makes defending a pre-set exchange rate level in a globalised market close to impossible.\par \par \uc2  Finally, as a member of the Group of Seven club of rich nations Japan has certain responsibilities, given the group's stated commitment to market-determined exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Possible Japan response to Swiss move         \tab \par Graphic on world rates       \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xuc92s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xuc92s}}}\uc2 \f2    \tab \par Fed, BOJ balance sheets      \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zum33s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zum33s}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Finance Minister Jun Azumi probably found out himself how\par difficult it is for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to gain consent even for unilateral\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when he met his G7 counterparts last week, some of\par whom have expressed discomfort over Tokyo's action last month.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Some analysts suggest the BOJ could help weaken the yen by\par adding foreign bonds to the list of assets it buys.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  But the BOJ is loath to do this because any effective action\par would require buying huge amounts, exposing its balance sheet to\par considerable risk. Such action would also impinge on the finance\par ministry's jurisdiction. \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  NOT OFF THE HOOK\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has played down the possible impact of\par Swiss efforts to curb the franc, and market action so far\par suggests that a feared yen rally on safe-haven flows has not yet\par materialised.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Still, jitters over Europe's debt crisis and expectations\par that the U.S. Federal Reserve will further loosen its policy\par could spur more flows into the yen.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  While Japan has plenty of its own economic problems, the\par depth of its financial markets and the relative stability of its\par financing costs makes it an attractive option for those seeking\par a safe home for their investments.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Another yen test of its record high could be more painful\par for Japan than last month, with the global slowdown now seen as\par more pronounced and no end in sight to Europe's debt crisis.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  That could force the BOJ to abandon its forecast of a\par moderate recovery by year-end when it issues long-term growth\par forecasts next month.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  A revision at a time when parliament will debate how to fund\par the main batch of reconstruction spending could spur calls from\par lawmakers for more aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Among the steps suggested by lawmakers, including senior\par ruling party officials, are an aggressive balance sheet\par expansion, increased purchases of long-term government bonds and\par even direct underwriting of government debt.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda, who as finance minister\par avoided leaving the impression that he was leaning on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , may pay more heed to such calls and become more\par vocal in demanding further monetary stimulus, some analysts say.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "The Federal Reserve may ease this month and the Swiss took\par bold steps on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The BOJ might end up being the only\par major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  not doing anything," said Takeshi Minami,\par chief economist at Norinchukin Research Institute in Tokyo.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "If several events drive the yen up again, the BOJ will be\par under pressure to act with Noda seeming very concerned about the\par risk of yen rises on the economy."\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  There is a debate within the BOJ on what more it can do\par beyond boosting its asset-buying programme, and some do not rule\par out steps such as more aggressive bond buying as an option if\par the economy worsens further.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  But there is no consensus within the BOJ on whether the\par benefits of such moves outweigh the drawbacks. Governor Masaaki\par Shirakawa is among the sceptics and said after the last policy\par meeting that the bank has already put powerful monetary easing\par in place to hedge against potential risks.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Yet more market turmoil and fresh safe-haven flows may force\par the BOJ's hand.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "If yen rises and a global downturn hit Japan at the same\par time, the BOJ would be in a tight spot," said another source\par familiar with the BOJ's thinking. "It is not complacent because\par it knows the market's tide can change any time."\tab \par \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/BOJ (ANALYSIS, CORRECTED)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110917e79e0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
