\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  COLUMN-Exporters' struggles may require BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2011\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 -- Jeremy Boulton is an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market analyst for Reuters. The opinions expressed are his own --\par \par \uc2 By Jeremy Boulton\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 13 (Reuters) - The financial half-year end in Japan on Sept. 31 could be the spur for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, which is hovering close to 2011 highs against the euro and sterling.\par \par \uc2 If the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's prior \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Aug. 4 was designed as a smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it was initially fairly successful. Dollar/yen has rarely dropped below the 76.96 yen low seen on Aug. 4.\par \par \uc2 However, viewed more broadly, the yen has strengthened, alarmingly so for Japan's exporters, who will probably be praying for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action before their books close.\par \par \uc2 Given the high volume of Japanese trade with the UK and Europe, the yen's rise to 2011 peaks just ahead of the financial half-year end could persuade the authorities to act.\par \par \uc2 After all there has been no reaction to all the other monetary policy measures the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has adopted in order to try and stem yen gains.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ and \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also be influenced by the success of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's policy to weaken the franc.\par \par \uc2 Although economists and analysts make a good case for why the BOJ will not copy the SNB, it seems size does matter in markets. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders have not challenged the SNB pledge to buy unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to set a floor for euro/Swiss.\par \par \uc2 Should the Bank of Japan take that as a sign of success, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may conclude that much larger sales of yen may also be needed in order to turn market sentiment towards the yen.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ may not want to draw a line in the sand as the SNB has done, but it could look to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the swaps market -- a policy that was successful for the SNB before it decided to deploy the nuclear option in its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war.\par \par \uc2 Whatever action Japan's authorities take, positioning data suggests the BOJ has a good chance of short-term success. Data from the Commodity Futures Trading Commission shows that specs are long yen to the equivalent of $5.0 billion .\par \par \uc2 Should the BOJ sell the yen, specs may initially cover positions in order to preserve profits. But if the BOJ can weaken the yen sufficiently, specs will instead need to limit losses.\par \par \uc2 While the chance to squeeze out speculators is probably not enough to make the BOJ to act, bolstering exporters' balance sheets at half-year end by providing them with better hedging rates might be.\par \par \uc2 Although the Japanese authorities usually say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prompted by moves that were either very rapid or out of line with fundamentals, many traders say action is more often than not designed to weaken the yen so that exporters can buy it.\par \par \uc2 Both major yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August 2011 an September 2010 seemed to run out of steam shortly after the bulk of exporter orders were filled.\par \par \uc2 Another possible sign of imminent action is that Japan's investors emerged with a sizeable bid for foreign bonds last week . Similar flows have preceded other \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If the BOJ does move to weaken the yen, it would probably not only squeeze out speculators, but also add to exporters' profits at vital time.\par \par \uc2 If intended as a continuation of the smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may again be relatively successful.\par \par \uc2 (Reuters Messaging: jeremy.boulton.thomsonreuters.com@reuters.net)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /YEN (\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  COLUMN)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110916e79d000rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
