\par\par \b \uc2 Japan MOF Official: Azumi Asked Geithner To Understand Yen Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2011\par 10:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MARSEILLE, France -(Dow Jones)- Japan's Finance Minister Jun Azumi asked his U.S. counterpart to understand his concerns over the yen's "one-sided" movement during their one-on-one meeting held on Saturday, a senior official from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "Japan's economy is in a steady recovery trend after the [March 11] earthquake," the official quoted Azumi as saying to U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner. "However, because of the recently one-sided movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Japanese industries are suffering significantly, and I am very concerned about downside risks. I think that the secretary is already well aware of this, but I'd like you to understand this point."\par \par \uc2 Yet, during the 15-minute meeting, Azumi didn't mention \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when it sees undue yen rises, the official said.\par \par \uc2 Azumi and Geithner both shared a strong interest in fiscal overhaul, and they agreed that advanced economies are responsible for undertaking fiscal reforms, the official said.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com [ 09-10-11 0427ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020110910e79a00007\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
