\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 9\b0\par\par\uc2 1,277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2011\par 09:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: CHINA AUGUST INFLATION MODERATES; GROWTH SLOWDOWN CONTINUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's inflation moderated in August, raising market hopes the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is done with tightening policy, although inflation remains at a relatively high level. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: JAPAN 2Q GDP SHRINKS MORE THAN INITIALLY REPORTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese economy contracted more severely than previously reported in the April-June period, data released Friday showed, with firms cutting back on capital spending at a faster pace in the wake of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami. (published 0309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FUJIMURA: CABINET TO WORK WITH OPPOSITION TO AID COS COPING WITH STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Friday that the government must gain opposition cooperation to promptly tackle the effect of the high yen on Japanese businesses. (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN ECON MIN FURUKAWA: NEED TO PAY CLOSE ATTENTION TO OVERSEAS ECON, YEN RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Friday that while the economy has picked up as supply-side constraints have eased, it is necessary to keep a careful watch on overseas economies and the yen's rise. (published 0151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PLANS TO INFORM G-7 OF ITS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Thursday he will inform top finance officials from the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations about his intention to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if he spots "excessive" speculation bolstering the yen. (published 0010 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER SIGNALS NO NEW CAPITAL FLOW STEPS IN NEAR TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Friday signaled that Asia's fourth-largest economy won't take any new action on managing foreign capital flows in the near term, emphasizing the need to preserve systemic stability. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN TSAI PICKS EX-INTERIOR MINISTER AS VICE-PRESIDENTIAL RUNNING MATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tsai Ing-wen, the presidential candidate for Taiwan's opposition Democratic Progressive Party, said Friday she had picked Su Jia-chyuan, a former interior minister, as her vice-presidential running mate for the election in January. (published 0612 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MAY LAUNCH PROGRAM FOR INVESTING OFFSHORE YUAN THIS MONTH - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China may launch the so-called "yuan-denominated foreign direct investment" program this month, the China Securities Journal reported Friday, citing Chinese Commerce Ministry spokesman Shen Danyang. (published 2334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MALAYSIA JULY INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT SHRINKS UNEXPECTEDLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's industrial output unexpectedly contracted in July, as the export-reliant nation's key manufacturing sector slowed on weak global demand while mining output continued to shrink. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN POWER RAISES NT$12 BLN IN BOND SALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the island's state-owned power producer and largest issuer of corporate bonds, said Friday it raised NT$12 billion via a bond sale. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN REGULATOR ACCC TO APPEAL COURT JUDGMENT ON METCASH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's competition watchdog said Friday it will appeal a court judgment throwing out its bid to block grocery wholesale and distribution company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Metcash Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . from acquiring supermarket chain Franklins for about A$215 million . (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: ANGLO SHUNS MACARTHUR COAL BID \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Anglo American PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has walked away from a potential counter bid for Australian coal miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macarthur Coal Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., deciding the price was ultimately too high, people familiar with the matter said. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: RIO TINTO TO INVEST US$310M IN WESTERN AUSTRALIA WATER SUPPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday it will invest US$310 million to ensure it has a sustainable water supply for its iron ore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the remote Pilbara region of Western Australia, where it plans to significantly boost output of the steelmaking commodity. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA YURUN: STRICTLY IMPLEMENT NATIONAL CONTROLLING TESTING STANDARDS ON PORK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Yurun Food Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday the company conducts tests on each of its hogs, strictly adheres to China's controls on pork, and implements national testing standards. (published 0048 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITIGROUP: NO LAYOFF PLAN FOR ASIA PACIFIC INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY DEPARTMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citigroup Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday there is no plan at the moment to lay off staff in its information technology department in Asia Pacific. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: NOMURA BOOSTS AUSTRALIAN OFFICE; TARGETS RESOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At a time when investment banks around the world are cutting staff, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nomura Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is building up its business in Australia announcing Friday four director-level hires. (published 0302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par POSCO MULLS RAISING STAKE IN BRAZIL'S NAMISA IRON ORE MINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Posco, the world's No. 3 steelmaker by output, said Friday that it is considering raising its stake in Brazil's Namisa iron ore mine as part of efforts to promote a stable supply of the key raw material. (published 0021 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par POWERCHIP: STRATEGICALLY CUT DRAM OUTPUT BY AT LEAST 50% IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dynamic random access memory chips maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Powerchip Technology Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it strategically reduced its DRAM output by at least 50% in August amid falling DRAM prices. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: UNITED ENERGY: SEEKING ASSETS IN MIDDLE EAST, NORTH AMERICA, SOUTH AMERICA, AUSTRALIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 United Energy Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., an investment company focused on upstream energy assets, said Friday it is seeking opportunities to acquire oil and gas assets in the Middle East, North and South America and Australia, as part of its strategy to boost production abroad. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIAN AIRLINE TO CONTINUE TO ENGAGE WITH UNIONS OVER AIRASIA PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian Airline System Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will continue to hold talks with employee unions over the collaborative agreement it signed with low-cost airline \f28 \uc2 \f2 AirAsia Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . last month. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TSMC AUGUST UNCONSOLIDATED REVENUE UP 1.5% AT NT$37.04 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s unconsolidated revenue rose 1.5% to NT$37.04 billion in August, from NT$36.50 billion a year earlier, it said Friday. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; CHINA INFLATION DATA PROVIDE FILLIP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares were mostly modestly higher in cautious, choppy trade Friday, coming off lows after Chinese data eased concerns about further tightening measures and after U.S. President Barack Obama's $447 billion plan to revive the U.S. economy. (published 0426 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA METALS OUTPUT RISES IN AUGUST; MORE DATA DUE TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's production of metals showed signs of robust year-on-year growth in August ahead of a peak season for the construction sector, with steel output rising 13% and nonferrous metals up 16%, the National Bureau of Statistics said Friday. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL DATA: CHINA AUGUST CRUDE RUNS 36.78 MLN TONS, UP 4.5% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China processed 36.78 million metric tons of crude oil last month, up 4.5% from a year earlier, data from the National Bureau of Statistics showed Friday. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: RIO TINTO TO INVEST US$310M IN WESTERN AUSTRALIA WATER SUPPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday it will invest US$310 million to ensure it has a sustainable water supply for its iron ore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the remote Pilbara region of Western Australia, where it plans to significantly boost output of the steelmaking commodity. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINOPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  INKS PACT WITH HUNAN GOVT ON REFINERY UPGRADE, PIPELINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Petroleum & Chemical Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., known as Sinopec, said Thursday that it has signed a preliminary agreement with the Hunan government on upgrading two refineries, building a natural gas pipeline and speeding up shale gas exploration. (published 0411 GMT) [ 09-09-11 0706GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110909e799000kg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
