\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 683 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2011\par 05:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA INFLATION MODERATES IN AUGUST; POLICY LIKELY ON HOLD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's inflation moderated in August, raising market hopes the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is done with tightening policy, although inflation remains at a relatively high level. (published 0214 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECON MIN FURUKAWA: NEED TO PAY CLOSE ATTENTION TO OVERSEAS ECON, YEN RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Friday that while the economy has picked up as supply-side constraints have eased, it is necessary to keep a careful watch on overseas economies and the yen's rise. (published 0151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PLANS TO INFORM G-7 OF ITS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Thursday he will inform top finance officials from the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations about his intention to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if he spots "excessive" speculation bolstering the yen. (published 0010 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN'S GDP SHRINKS MORE THAN INITIALLY REPORTED IN 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese economy contracted more severely than previously reported in the April-June period, data released Friday showed, with firms cutting back on capital spending at a faster pace in the wake of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami. (published 0037 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: BERNANKE SAYS FED STANDS READY TO ACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said Thursday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has the tools to provide more support to the sluggish U.S. economy, but declined to say whether it is prepared to use them in less than two weeks. (published 2039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB STARK: PREPARED TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS LONG AS LOW INTEREST RATES NOT TRANSLATED INTO LENDING RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jurgen Stark, Germany's representative on the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's executive board, said the ECB remains ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and its measures will remain in place as long as they need to be. (published 0048 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: SWISS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STANCE LIKE 'DRINKING POISON TO END THIRST' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stance won't work, and the bank may be forced to use capital controls and tax levies to stem speculative money inflows after any such action, People's Bank of China adviser Li Daokui said late Thursday. (published 0042 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA MAY LAUNCH PROGRAM FOR INVESTING OFFSHORE YUAN THIS MONTH - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China may launch the so-called "yuan-denominated foreign direct investment" program this month, the China Securities Journal reported Friday, citing Chinese Commerce Ministry spokesman Shen Danyang. (published 2334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: NZ AUGUST ADJ RETAIL SALES CARD TRANSACTIONS -0.7% ON MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand seasonally adjusted retail sales card transactions eased in August, data from Statistics New Zealand showed Friday, underscoring the fragile nature of the domestic economic recovery. (published 2256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: OBAMA URGES CONGRESS TO IMMEDIATELY PASS $447B JOBS PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama on Thursday proposed a $447 billion plan to revive the U.S. economy, saying his plan will provide an instant boost to the economy if Congress immediately passes it. (published 2340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SENATE VOTE MEANS THAT US BORROWING LIMIT IS IMMEDIATELY HIKED BY $500B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. Senate defeated an attempt by Republicans to slow down a $500 billion increase in the federal government's borrowing limit in a vote that means the borrowing limit is immediately hiked to $15.19 trillion. (published 0039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: SWISS CAP MOVE RILES OFFICIALS IN NORWAY, CANADA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Norwegian and Canadian officials on Thursday criticized Switzerland's move this week to cap the rise of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as the impact reverberated in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets world-wide. (published 2308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DRAGHI WELCOMES ITALY'S AUSTERITY PACKAGE - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi, Italy's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor and future European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  head, welcomed the Italian government's austerity plan which was approved by the Senate on Wednesday, Italian news agency Ansa reported Thursday. (published 2314 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par FED WATCH: FED'S PLOSSER SEES BENEFIT IN A MORE FOCUSED FED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stick to your knitting. That's the way the leader of the Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia, Charles Plosser, believes central banking should be done. (published 2002 GMT) [ 09-09-11 0302GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110909e7990007w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
