\par\par \b \uc2 Euro Falls Below Pre- \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  Levels Vs. Yen Below 106.50\b0\par\par\uc2 163 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2011\par 17:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--A battered euro sank to its weakest level in a year against the Japanese yen Friday, as markets grew increasingly unnerved about Europe's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 With the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  already hunkered at its deepest trough against the dollar since late February near $1.37, the euro tumbled as low as Y106.31. That was below the point when the Group of Seven staged a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen in mid-March.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of full-fledged euro zone debt contagion soured risk appetite, and pushed stocks sharply lower in morning U.S. trading. Analysts also say that a shift away from hiking interest rates by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also undermining the euro's yield-appeal.\par \par \uc2 -By Javier E. David, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-4564;\par \par \uc2 javier.david@dowjones.com [ 09-09-11 1118ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110909e79900089\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
