\par\par \b \uc2 Trichet's Preference For Chocolate Over Sushi Is Buy-Yen Signal\b0\par\par\uc2 By Vincent Cignarella  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2011\par 15:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Japan's government might have thought that the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's dramatic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week would breed international sympathy for its desire to do similarly with the yen.\par \par \uc2 But judging from the remarkably contradictory comments of European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet on Thursday, it seems pretty clear that Jun Azumi, Japan's new finance minister, will find few sympathizers among his counterparts at a Group of Seven meeting Friday. Azumi is likely to leave this event with the same message the G7 gave to his predecessor, Yoshihiko Noda, the man who is now Prime Minister: you're on your own.\par \par \uc2 And if that's the case, there's a signal to buy yen in there.\par \par \uc2 In the press conference following the ECB's decision to keep rates on hold Thursday, Trichet offered what will surely be seen as a double standard by Japan's government.\par \par \uc2 While he described the SNB's unilateral decision to drastically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a "decision we respect," he was far less complimentary of Japan's move in August to soften the yen.\par \par \uc2 Citing the "very clear position in the Governing Council of the ECB," Trichet said that "such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have to be made on a multilateral consensus and [as a] multilateral decision."\par \par \uc2 In case the point wasn't clear, he added, "To my knowledge [\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August] is not part of a multilateral decision."\par \par \uc2 This will hardly be welcome news for Azumi, whose primary mission at Friday's G7 get-together in Marseille is to win a statement of support for Japan's view that yen appreciation is excessive and doesn't match with the fundamental economics of Japan.\par \par \uc2 Beyond the question of policymaker doublespeak, Trichet's comments offer a signal to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders. By default, the ECB chief said that selling CHF/JPY is OK with him.\par \par \uc2 Without G7 support, unilateral Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is futile. So in my view we have a clear opportunity to bet that the yen will continue to gain against both the EUR and the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 (Vincent Cignarella is a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist/journalist for DJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trader. His 30 years in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets include working as a bank dealer at major money-center commercial banks; managing corporate-hedging for a large multinational; serving as a principal and general partner of a major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage firm; and most recently working in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales with Santander in New York. He can be reached at vincent.cignarella@dowjones.com) [ 09-09-11 0909ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110909e7990007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
