\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ: Japan Quashes Speculation Of Yen Ceiling\b0\par\par\uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2011\par 13:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Finance Ministry says no move to place a ceiling on yen's value\par \par \uc2 --Igarashi says Japan must not provoke \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war\par \par \uc2 --Comments sent yen sharply lower versus dollar, euro\par \par \uc2 (Updates with fresh yen quote in paragraph 5, Azumi comment in paragraph 6, and analyst comment in paragraphs 12 and 13)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of THE WALL STREET JOURNAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese Finance Ministry officials on Wednesday quashed any ideas that Japan may follow the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trying to place a ceiling on the value of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappointed some in the market who had expected further easing by leaving rates unchanged.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Japan must construct policies from the viewpoint of respecting, protecting and promoting growth of an open market as we have the world's third-largest economy and third-most-important \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Senior Vice Finance Minister Fumihiko Igarashi at a news conference. "Japan must not provoke a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war by itself."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Igarashi's comments came after Finance Minister Jun Azumi shrugged off speculation following the action announced Tuesday by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Switzerland is Switzerland," Azumi said when asked what he thought of the Swiss move.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This story and related background material will be available on The Wall Street Journal website, WSJ.com.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday set a ceiling on the franc's level against the euro and said it is ready to launch unlimited \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaigns to keep it from rising above that level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The move sent the yen sharply lower against the dollar and euro. Wednesday afternoon in Japan, the dollar was at JPY77.29, up from around JPY76.70 before the Swiss announcement, but still near its post-war record low of JPY75.94 reached in August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Japan is facing difficult conditions at this point because of the strong yen. We are watching market moves, including those by speculators," Azumi said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Like the Swiss franc, the yen has seen strong flight-to-safety flows amid a bleak outlook for the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders had been looking to the Bank of Japan for further monetary easing that would help push the yen lower, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy board ended a two-day meeting on Wednesday with no new measures. The bank's policy board voted unanimously to leave its policy rate--the unsecured overnight call loan rate--in a 0.0%-0.1% range.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite their concerns, government officials have been quick to note the difficulties in attempting to put a ceiling on the yen's rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As a G-7 nation, Japan needs to be committed to a free-floating exchange rate and would likely face renewed criticism even if it undertook another round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Analysts say this is particularly true ahead of this weekend's meeting of G-7 finance ministers in France.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese officials have also said that the yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is about three times the size of trading in the Swiss franc. One official said that putting a peg in place would require a country to either impose capital restrictions or effectively abandon its monetary policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts have also widely dismissed the idea. Tohru Sasaki, chief strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Tokyo, pointed out that such a peg requires massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is not cost-free and would add to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If the MOF conducts unlimited \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it means that the Japanese government debt may increase without limit--something that the government really needs to avoid," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 So far, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is in charge of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy in Japan, has announced less-aggressive measures to curb the yen's rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Last month, the ministry said it will ask major banks to report their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  positions on a daily basis in a possible attempt to create a psychological brake on speculative trading. While trying to combat the strong yen, the Japanese government also appears resigned to its continued rise, shifting its focus to helping companies take advantage of the yen's strength.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Megumi Fujikawa contributed to this article. [ 09-07-11 0809ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110907e7970003n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
