\par\par \b \uc2 FXNEWS-ASIA OPEN-Euro bounces ahead of ECB\b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2011\par 00:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Euro up modestly in early Asia after high-court decision to clear the way for German participation in bailouts gave an excuse for markets to buy risk assets. Euro at $1.4095 , having hit $1.4148 offshore. ECB rate decision due at 1145GMT with markets certain the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep rates steady. Single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could receive another kick if Trichet doesn't sound as dovish as some think though deciphering his words can be tricky. Major resistance seen at around $1.4200, the 38.2 Fibo of the $1.4550/$1.3972 move. Euro stayed well above the 1.20 francs line in the sand drawn by the SNB. Last at 1.2087 francs. \par \par \uc2  USD index 0.6 pct lower at 75.490. Dollar at 77.30 yen as improved risk appetite delayed downside test. Markets had thought \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might follow the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lead to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Australian dollar, among the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Last trades at $1.0650, having gained 1.5 pct in 24 hours. Key flashpoint is on Australian jobs data at 0130GMT with expectations of 11,000 jobs being added and jobless rate steady at 5.1 pct. Anything weaker could see the Aussie retreat again. \par \par \uc2  RM: cecile.lefort.thomsonreuters.com@reuters.net\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110907e7970014a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
