\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar, Yen Firm In Asia After SNB Move\b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2011\par 03:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Dollar firm in early Asian trading following surprise Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move\par \par \uc2 -- Market quiet after a volatile Tuesday with traders absorbing news\par \par \uc2 -- Yen resumes strengthening trend after sharp fall late Tuesday on Swiss news\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Kosaku Narioka \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar and yen were firm in early Asian trading Wednesday as the market recalibrated following a surprise announcement by the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to set a ceiling for the Swiss franc.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There will be a lot of very burnt people overnight. Everyone is going to be licking their wounds, so it may be a day of going sideways," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 HiFX\f28 \uc2 \f2  senior trader Stuart Ive in Auckland.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  announcement, he and other traders cited a litany of market worries for the dollar's firmness, including a strike in Italy, protests in Spain and Greece's debt problems amid increasing opposition in Germany to boosting euro-zone rescue efforts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of 0100 GMT, the euro was at $1.4024, according to data from EBS, from $1.3997 in late New York trade. Against the yen, the euro was little changed at Y108.62 from Y108.70.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar trended lower against the yen after a morning high of Y77.71, with some traders waiting to see if Japan, as one of the few remaining safe havens, would follow on the Swiss action with steps of its own to help contain the strength of the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan concludes a two-day policy board meeting later in the day and the market will be looking for any additional easing steps that would add to its balance sheet and, theoretically at least, help lower the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's value.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was at Y77.46 as of 0100 GMT, from Y77.66 in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar may fall below Y77.00 after the BOJ meeting later in the day, said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Barclays Bank in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Given recent weaker Japanese economic indicators, concerns over a global economic slowdown and the Nikkei Stock Average approaching 8000, the BOJ can take an additional easing steps, he said. Still, any likely BOJ action would be to expand its asset-purchase program by Y5 trillion to Y10 trillion. This "would likely lead to disappointment," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One senior dealer at a major European bank in Tokyo said, though, that the market would become cautious in any fall below Y77.00 for the dollar in the view that could prompt renewed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss franc meanwhile remained near its newly established ceiling, with the euro at CHF1.2055 from CHF1.2070 in New York. The dollar was at CHF0.8591 from CHF0.8625.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The British pound was at $1.5950 from $1.5946, while the ICE Dollar Index was at 75.795 from 75.929.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 20:50 EDT / 0050 GMT \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            77.51-52       77.64-69  -0.20    77.70    77.44  -4.44 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.4018-20      1.3996-99  +0.15   1.4025   1.3994  +4.69 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5944-48      1.5942-53  -0.01   1.5966   1.5934  +2.17 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.8604-08      0.8613-28  -0.17   0.8623   0.8596  -7.96 \par USD/CAD Canada         0.9895-900      0.9901-05  -0.06   0.9905   0.9892  -0.50 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0531-36      1.0482-87  +0.47   1.0542   1.0484  +2.93 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.8252-56      0.8224-29  +0.33   0.8261   0.8224  +5.87 \par  \par Euro Rate \par EUR/JPY Japan           108.65-68      108.67-74  -0.04   108.75   108.58  +0.03 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Kosaku Narioka, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2784; kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com [ 09-06-11 2145ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020110907e7970000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
