\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Japan Won't Follow SNB Lead -\uc2 JPMorgan\b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2011\par 13:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1153 GMT [Dow Jones] Bank of Japan will not follow SNB, says \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 , citing four key reasons. First, Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is conducted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which will want to avoid unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the knock-on effect on government debt. Second, MOF involvement makes it difficult for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward market as the SNB has done and with the ample liquidity in the JPY funding market, it is difficult for the BOJ to justify the rationale of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards. Third, the government is not happy with BOJ losses caused by JPY appreciation and current conditions give the government no incentive to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  take \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks rather than the MOF. Fourth, total daily JPY turnover in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is about three times larger than CHF, so it is risky for the Japanese government to conduct such a huge \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/JPY now at 77.26. (jessica.mead@dowjones.com) Contact us in London: +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 06-09-11 1153GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110906e796000vx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw1