\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: More Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , BOJ Easing By End-Sept -Nomura\b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2011\par 03:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0151 GMT [Dow Jones] Nomura Securities says it expects Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  easing action in concert with government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign exhange market and measures to tackle the strong yen. Nomura now seens the Bank of Japan taking additional monetary policy steps in August or September, compared with a previous assumption of Q4. "With the yen having appreciated at a faster-than-expected pace of late, we think the BOJ looks increasingly likely to bring forward easing steps in concert with the Japanese government's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," writes house analyst Takahide Kiuchi. He adds that further easing will take the form of a Y3 trillion-Y5 trillion expansion of BOJ asset purchases. The house also expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase its asset purchases by Y3 trillion-Y5 trillion in 2011 Q4. The yen's rise has been a major factor in recent Japan stock sell-offs. Further policy-easing may help by encouraging more risk-taking via equity investing. (bradford.frischkorn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 25-08-11 0151GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 5011 55117   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110825e78p0004i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
