\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Yen Holds Steady In Subdued Trading Session\b0\par\par\uc2 781 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2011\par 13:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Yen holds steady as traders fear \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- Dollar mixed ahead of Friday's eagerly anticipated Jackson Hole speech\par \par \uc2 -- Swiss franc weakness persists\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Clare Connaghan \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON -(Dow Jones)- \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets were relatively subdued during European trading hours Monday with the euro locked into a trading range against the dollar, while the yen held steady against the buck as traders braced for fresh action by Japan to tame the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister, who controls decisions on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , stepped up his rhetoric against the yen's strength Monday, saying recent "one-sided yen moves" have been accelerating.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We will not rule out any possible measure and will take decisive steps if needed," Yoshihiko Noda said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 His comments were enough to stop traders jumping into the yen in European trading hours, as market participants remain on high alert of government action, particularly since the dollar marked a fresh post World War II-low at Y75.94 Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "People are afraid there is going to be an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Sebastien Galy, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1046 GMT, the dollar was at Y76.790 against the yen, compared with Y76.54, while the euro was at Y110.827 compared with Y110.20.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More broadly, the picture was mixed with the dollar losing ground against the commodity-linked \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Australia, New Zealand and Canada.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We're in a range trading environment," said Galy, adding market participants are selling the dollar but "with extreme caution."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This could persist until Friday when Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke's gives his annual speech at Jackson Hole, Wyoming.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The past three or four Jackson Hole meetings have been instrumental in shaping the policy response to the crisis and in providing hints to markets about what was to come," said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Bank of Scotland\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategists Silvio Peruzzo and Jan Dubsky in a note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "With financial market conditions deteriorating rapidly and the risk of recession now a real one, Bernanke will no doubt feel it needs to shed new lights on the next potential policy steps," they added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ahead of that, Monday's data calendar is relatively light with only Chicago's Fed July National Activity Index reading due at 1230 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the euro was mostly higher across the board despite German Chancellor Angela Merkel repeating Sunday her rejection of collective euro bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The 17-country \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held onto gains against the Swiss franc amid ongoing concerns that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  could announce further measures to counter \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength. This might be working for now, but the market could lose patience soon and test the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's determination once again.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The longer the SNB hesitates the larger the number of market participants who will doubt the SNB's determination," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategists in a note to clients. "This process would slowly increase the pressure on the euro against the Swiss franc again."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1048 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.4433 against the dollar, compared with $1.4396 late Friday in New York, according to trading system EBS. The pound was at $1.64920 against the dollar, compared with $1.6479 late Friday in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 73.844 compared with 73.990 late Friday in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1052 GMT     1.4430     76.79      1.6501     0.7865 \par 3 Day Trend       Range      Bearish    Bearish    Range \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Bearish    Bullish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.4054     81.39      1.6113     0.8854 \par 3rd Resistance    1.4537     77.23      1.6617     0.7970 \par 2nd Resistance    1.4518     76.91      1.6592     0.7910 \par 1st Resistance    1.4453     76.86      1.6508     0.7892 \par Pivot*            1.4369     76.49      1.6514     0.7872 \par 1st Support       1.4393     76.67      1.6456     0.7839 \par 2nd Support       1.4347     76.56      1.6400     0.7807 \par 3rd Support       1.4319     76.24      1.6340     0.7680 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/GBP \par  \par Spot 1052 GMT     0.8747 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish \par Weekly Trend      Bearish \par 200 day ma        0.8720 \par 3rd Resistance    0.8841 \par 2nd Resistance    0.8829 \par 1st Resistance    0.8751 \par Pivot*            0.8715 \par 1st Support       0.8696 \par 2nd Support       0.8654 \par 3rd Support       0.8644 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0) 20 7842 9496, clare.connaghan@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Dow Jones Technical Strategist Francis Bray contributed to this article.) [ 08-22-11 0719ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020110822e78m0002m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
