\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 705 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2011\par 10:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN FINANCE MINISTRY: ECONOMIC GROWTH TO SLOW FOR REST OF 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's economic growth has experienced an "unexpected, obvious slowdown" that may continue through the end of 2011, the country's Finance Ministry said in a report released Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN NODA WON'T RULE OUT ANY POSSIBLE MEASURES TO COUNTER YEN STRENGTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Minister stepped up his rhetoric against the yen's strength Monday, saying the nation will not exclude any possible measures and take decisive steps to counter speculative moves.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  KAIEDA: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COULD HAVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AT TOKYO MARKET OPENING - REPORT \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's trade minister issued fresh warnings against speculators buying the yen, saying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by now today, the Sankei Shimbun reported Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EURO STABLE DESPITE DEBT CRISIS SAYS SCHAEUBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BERLIN: Despite the excessive debt levels in some euro-zone countries, the euro remains a stable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , German Finance Minister Wolfgang Schaeuble said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB'S NOWOTNY WORRIED EFSF CHANGES MAY BE DELAYED - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governing Council Member Ewald Nowotny says he is concerned that changes agreed in July to the European Financial Stability Facility won't be ratified by November as planned, the weekly magazine Profil reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  S&P: 'NO MATH ERROR' IN US RATING CUT, NO QUALMS ABOUT MORE ACTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit rating firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Monday again defended its recent decision to downgrade the U.S.'s sovereign credit rating and said market volatility would not deter it from other rating cuts when justified.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S: EURO-ZONE MEMBERS' RETICENCE PUTS PRESSURE ON FRANCE, GERMANY TO PROTECT EMU \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The reticence of some euro-zone policy makers to act to protect the stability of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bloc puts pressure on France and Germany to take more aggressive steps than their recent proposals, a senior analyst at Moody's Investors Service said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TAIWAN JULY JOBLESS RATE EDGES UP TO 4.41% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's jobless rate edged up in July as more school graduates entered the job market, the Directorate-General of Budget, Accounting and Statistics said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI GDP SHRINKS IN 2Q; GOVERNMENT TRIMS 2011 GROWTH FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai economy contracted in the second quarter as supply disruptions in the auto industry caused by the natural disasters in Japan took its toll on Southeast Asia's second-largest economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HK JULY HEADLINE CPI +7.9%; EXPECTED +8.2% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's headline consumer price index in July rose 7.9% from a year earlier, but the reading was distorted by a low base of comparison due to government relief measures last July, the Census and Statistics Department said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER, OFFICIAL ADD TO ECONOMIC POLICY DEBATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should take measures to spur the domestic economy instead of cooling it as the ongoing U.S. debt crisis will affect the Asian country, Wang Jian, secretary general of the National Development and Reform Commission's macroeconomic research unit, wrote in an article in the China Securities Journal Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER FLAGS RISKS TO 2011 GROWTH, INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Monday signaled risks to the government's 2011 growth and inflation forecasts, underscoring difficulties faced by Asia's fourth-largest economy amid persistent inflation and heightened external uncertainties.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ:THAI POLITICIAN'S TRIP TO JAPAN STIRS QUESTIONS FOR SISTER'S GOVERNMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ousted Thai leader Thaksin Shinawatra's rush back onto the international stage with a trip to Japan scheduled to begin Monday is raising awkward questions for his sister, recently elected Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra, about who really runs the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA DEVELOPMENT BANK TO SELL CNY36 BLN BILLS, BONDS THURSDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Development Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it plans to auction CNY16 billion worth of one-year bills and CNY20 billion worth of three-year floating-rate bonds Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: SINGAPORE JULY CPI LIKELY 5.0%; PRICES MAY BE FIRMING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's consumer prices likely remained at elevated levels because of a tight local labor market and rising commodity prices, prompting economists to warn that inflation momentum in the island nation may be picking up again. (published 0320 GMT) [ 22-08-11 0858GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110822e78m000ni\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
