\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan Noda says to act decisively, won't rule out any steps on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2011\par 01:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Watching for any speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves -Noda\par \par \uc2 * Will exchange information closely with other countries on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds quote, details)\par \par \uc2 By Kaori Kaneko\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 22 (Reuters) - Japan will take decisive action against any speculative moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said on Monday, signalling Tokyo's readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem further yen rises in the wake of its spike to a record high against the dollar last week.\par \par \uc2 Noda said he saw recent yen rises as even more one-sided than before and that Tokyo would exchange information closely with other countries regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We will watch markets even more closely than before to see whether there is any speculative activity. We won't rule out any measures and will take decisive action when necessary," Noda told reporters.\par \par \uc2 He also repeated that the government would work closely with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the economy.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  unilaterally in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and eased monetary policy on Aug. 4. But the steps have not stopped investors from seeking the yen as a safe haven against risk, with the dollar hitting a record low of 75.95 yen last Friday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar is now hovering around 76.85 yen with market expectations of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeping investors from testing the downside, at least for now.\par \par \uc2 The government may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unilaterally again in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the yen rise accelerates. The BOJ is ready to support any such yen-weakening attempts and will consider easing policy, possibly before its next rate review in September, if yen gains push down Tokyo stock prices enough to hit business sentiment, sources familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking have said.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Leika Kihara; Editing by Edmund Klamann)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/NODA  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110824e78l0017b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
